sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Trader
    participant CD as CyberDeltaEngine
    participant ML as ML Module (Inactive)
    participant FRS as Funding Rate Strategy
    participant BP as Backpack API (CEX)
    participant HL as Hyperliquid API (DEX)
    participant PX as Paradex API (DEX)
    participant RM as Risk Management
    participant OR as External Oracle

    Note over CD,RM: Initialization Phase
    User->>CD: Initialize trading bot (Funding Rate Strategy Only)
    CD->>FRS: Set funding rate parameters (thresholds, lookback periods)
    CD->>RM: Configure static risk limits (VaR_0=$10k, CVaR_0=$15k, MaxPos=$50k)
    CD->>RM: Enable dynamic risk adjustment (VaR_t = VaR_0 * (σ_mkt_t / σ_mkt_0))
    Note right of RM: σ_mkt_t from 1h rolling window, σ_mkt_0 = historical avg
    CD->>ML: Load ML models (inactive, for future use)
    CD->>CD: Log initialization details (timestamp, params)

    Note over CD,PX: Data Collection & Validation Phase
    loop Every 5s: Collect Market Data
        par Fetch CEX Data
            CD->>BP: Request perp prices, funding rates, oracle data, order book depth
            BP-->>CD: Backpack Market Data (e.g., BTC-PERP: P=$60k, FR=0.01%, Depth=$1M)
        and Fetch DEX Data (Hyperliquid)
            CD->>HL: Request perp prices, funding rates, oracle/mark data, depth
            HL-->>CD: Hyperliquid Market Data (e.g., BTC-PERP: P=$60.1k, FR=0.015%, Depth=$800k)
        and Fetch DEX Data (Paradex)
            CD->>PX: Request perp prices, funding rates, oracle/mark data, depth
            PX-->>CD: Paradex Market Data (e.g., BTC-PERP: P=$59.9k, FR=0.012%, Depth=$900k)
        and Fetch Backup Data
            CD->>OR: Request external oracle prices (e.g., Chainlink)
            OR-->>CD: Oracle Data (e.g., BTC: P=$60.05k)
        end
        CD->>CD: Validate data: Check timestamps (Δt < 10s), price consistency (|P_X - P_OR| < 3σ_spread)
        Note right of CD: If validation fails (e.g., stale BP data), use OR avg or pause pair
    end

    Note over CD,RM: Analysis Phase
    CD->>FRS: Input validated data from BP, HL, PX
    FRS->>FRS: Calc basis volatility per pair/exchange: σ_B,t = √(Σ(P_t - P_{t-1})^2 / n)
    FRS->>FRS: Calc single-exchange profit: π^X = FR^X - (Fee^X + Slippage^X + Gas^X)
    Note right of FRS: Slippage^X = β * (Order_Size / Depth), β=0.1
    FRS->>FRS: Calc cross-exchange profit: π^{AB} = |FR^A - FR^B| - (C^A + C^B + NFD_adj)
    Note right of FRS: NFD_adj = Net Funding Differential * Latency_Factor
    FRS-->>CD: Output arbitrage signals (π^X, π^{AB}, σ_B,t)
    CD->>RM: Compute Kelly sizing: f* = (π / σ_B,t^2), apply α=0.5
    RM->>RM: Check risk: Portfolio variance √(w^T Σ w) <= MaxRisk, VaR_t <= VaR_limit
    Note right of RM: Σ updated hourly via rolling correlations
    RM-->>CD: Return position sizing (w_target) per opportunity
    CD->>CD: Rank by Utility: U = π - λ * σ_B,t^2, λ=1

    Note over CD,RM: Collateral Check / Rebalancing Phase
    RM->>BP: Query collateral: C_current^BP vs C_target^BP (e.g., $100k vs $110k)
    RM->>HL: Query collateral: C_current^HL vs C_target^HL (e.g., $90k vs $100k)
    RM->>PX: Query collateral: C_current^PX vs C_target^PX (e.g., $80k vs $90k)
    alt Collateral deviation > 10% or trade requires funds
        RM->>RM: Optimize transfer: Min(Cost + Delay), e.g., BP->HL: $20k
        par Execute Transfers
            RM->>BP: Withdraw $20k USDC (API call)
            BP-->>RM: Withdrawal confirmation (ETA: 5min)
            RM->>HL: Deposit $20k USDC (via wallet, gas=$5)
            HL-->>RM: Deposit confirmation (on-chain)
        and Monitor
            RM->>CD: Track status, alert if delay > 10min
        end
    else Collateral sufficient
        RM-->>CD: No action needed
    end
    Note right of RM: Buffer: C_actual = C_target * 1.1

    Note over CD,User: Decision & Execution Phase
    CD->>CD: Select top opportunity (max U, latency-adjusted)
    alt Single-Exchange Arb (e.g., HL)
        CD->>HL: Place delta-neutral trade (Long Perp $50k, Short Spot $50k)
        Note over CD,HL: Captures FR=0.015%, Slippage=$50
    else Cross-Exchange Arb (e.g., BP vs HL)
        CD->>BP: Execute Leg 1: Short Perp $50k (FOK)
        CD->>HL: Execute Leg 2: Long Perp $50k (FOK)
        Note over CD,HL: Exploits FR diff: 0.01% vs 0.015%
    else Cross-Exchange Arb (e.g., HL vs PX)
        CD->>HL: Execute Leg 1: Short Perp $50k
        CD->>PX: Execute Leg 2: Long Perp $50k
    else Cross-Exchange Arb (e.g., BP vs PX)
        CD->>BP: Execute Leg 1: Short Perp $50k
        CD->>PX: Execute Leg 2: Long Perp $50k
    end
    CD->>RM: Update positions: Track open exposure per exchange
    RM->>RM: Calc real-time risk: VaR_t, CVaR_t, σ_P

    Note over CD,User: Monitoring & Adaptation Phase
    loop Every funding period (e.g., 8h BP, 1h HL/PX)
        par Collect Funding
            CD->>BP: Fetch funding payment (e.g., $50)
            BP-->>CD: Funding settled
            CD->>HL: Fetch funding payment (e.g., $75)
            HL-->>CD: Funding settled
            CD->>PX: Fetch funding payment (e.g., $60)
            PX-->>CD: Funding settled
        end
        CD->>CD: Update PnL: PnL_t = PnL_{t-1} + Funding - Costs
        CD->>CD: Calc Funding Yield: FY = Funding / Capital
    end
    loop Every 15min: Adapt
        CD->>FRS: Refresh σ_B,t, Fee^X, Gas^X
        FRS-->>CD: Updated estimates
        CD->>RM: Adjust w_target, VaR_t if Sharpe_t < 1
    end
    CD->>User: Report: PnL=$500, FY=0.5%, σ_P=0.02, VaR_t=$12k